# Chroma library, modern Earth: aims v1, group E's spark moments (earth_aims.py). Syntax: header of build.py.
# Build: python3 build.py earth_aim_moments. Nothing reads these until the Engine's aims switch is on.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to work the land (G; cycle s1)

== a first crop from a borrowed field
tier: life event
aim: to work the land
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 12-70
per_year: 0 .3 .5 .4 .3 0
times: while the aim is set, a first season on a patch of borrowed ground comes once or twice (estimate)
tone: mixed
life: work, nature
horizon: months
roles: elder, neighbour, friend
earth: a farmer down the lane lets you have the bottom corner of a field for one season
tribal: an elder gives you a strip of the clan's ground to sow and keep through one season
magic: the tower's gardener gives you one bed of the kitchen garden to keep through the summer
scene: {elder} from down the lane has let {N} have the bottom corner of a field for the season. The potatoes are in, the weeds are coming, and the rain has not.
scene W: {N} said the corner would be kept properly, and means it, every row of it.
scene U: {N} has a notebook already: the dates of planting, the last frost, a sketch of the rows.
scene B: {N} has worked out what a good crop would fetch at the farm shop, and wants it.
scene R: {N} cannot sit through a school or work day without thinking about the field.
scene G: {N} kneels at the edge of the rows at dawn, just to see what came up in the night.
- W | weed the rows every evening at the same hour, whatever the weather | v: conformity, security | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 72
- U | test the soil and log every planting and every frost | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | promise the whole crop to the farm shop before a single potato is up | v: achievement, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 55
- R | dig the whole corner in one wild weekend and plant everything at once | v: stimulation | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | learn the field by hand at dawn, one plant at a time | v: tradition, universalism | dream: test | foot: place prod.land | chance: 68
- W>U | ask the old farmer how this ground has always been worked, and copy it exactly | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- U>B | work out which crop would fetch the best price and grow only that | v: achievement | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 62
- B>R | trade a share of the harvest for help, and make a party of the digging | v: hedonism, power | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- R>G | sleep out by the rows the night a frost is forecast, with a fire going | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: lesson frost waits for nobody | chance: 58
- G>W | carry the first basket to every house down the lane | v: benevolence, tradition | dream: test | foot: person neighbour | chance: 74
works: The first basket comes up out of the ground heavy and clean, and {N} holds it a long moment.
works: {elder} walks the rows at the end of the season and says the corner has never looked better.
fails: A late frost takes half the rows in one night, and the rest come up small.
fails: The weeds win by late summer, and {N} digs up a crop hardly worth the carrying.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to keep the family's ways (G; cycle s1)

== the old dish made with nobody watching
tier: life event
aim: to keep the family's ways
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 13-90
per_year: 0 .3 .4 .4 .4 .3
times: while the aim is set, a family gathering where the old dish falls to the character comes once or twice (estimate)
tone: mixed
life: family, home
horizon: week
roles: grandparent, parent, sibling, cousins
earth: your grandparent is too frail this year to make the dish the family has at every gathering, and the kitchen is yours
tribal: the old woman who always cooks the feast-day roots is too weak this season, and the fire is yours
magic: the old aunt who brews the house's festival cordial is abed, and her copper and her spoon are yours
scene: {grandparent} is too frail this year to make the dish the family has at every gathering. The old pan is on the stove, the card in the drawer is half worn away, and the cousins arrive at six.
scene W: {N} wants it made exactly as it has always been made, because that is the point of it.
scene U: {N} has eaten it a hundred times and still cannot say what goes in it, and that bothers {N}.
scene B: The whole family will taste it and judge it, and {N} would like them impressed.
scene R: {N} has always thought the dish could be better, and nobody is here to stop the experiment.
scene G: The kitchen smells of {Ns} childhood before anything is even in the pan.
- W | follow the worn card exactly, down to the last pinch of salt | v: tradition, conformity | foot: lesson the old card knows best | chance: 70
- U | ring round the aunts and piece together how it was really made | v: self-direction, tradition | foot: person elder | chance: 72
- B | make it bigger and richer than it has ever been, to be talked about | v: achievement | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 60
- R | throw out the card and cook it the way it tastes in memory | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | cook it in the old pan the way the hands remember from childhood | v: tradition | dream: test | foot: place gather.house | chance: 66
- W>U | write the whole method down at last, so nobody has to guess again | v: tradition, universalism | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 78
- U>B | sell jars of it at the market under the family name | v: achievement, tradition | foot: place comm.market | chance: 55
- B>R | turn the gathering into a party and invite half the street | v: hedonism, power | foot: person neighbour | chance: 68
- R>G | run a plate up to the old cook's bed while it is still hot | v: benevolence, hedonism | foot: lesson a hot plate says enough | chance: 85
- G>W | sit the youngest cousins at the stove and teach them the family's way of it | v: tradition, benevolence | dream: seal | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 64
works: The first spoonful goes round the table, and the room goes quiet, the good kind of quiet.
works: {grandparent} tastes it from the bed and nods once, and that is enough.
fails: It comes out wrong, and everyone is kind about it, which is worse.
fails: The pan catches, the kitchen fills with smoke, and supper is bought from the shop on the corner.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to grow old among many grandchildren (G; cycle s4)

== the cousins all under one roof
tier: life event
aim: to grow old among many grandchildren
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 22-90
per_year: 0 0 .3 .4 .5 .5
times: while the aim is set, a weekend minding the whole family's children comes now and then (estimate)
tone: joy
life: family, home
horizon: week
roles: sibling, child, parent, the cousins' children
earth: the family leaves all its children with you for a long weekend
tribal: the clan's mothers and fathers go to the far meeting and leave every child at your fire
magic: the house's grown children ride to the city for the fair and leave the little ones in your wing
scene: {sibling} and the cousins have left all the children at {Ns} for the long weekend: seven of them, two dogs, one bathroom, and rain forecast for both days.
scene W: {N} wants every child fed, washed and in bed on time, all seven, every night.
scene U: {N} watches the seven of them sort themselves out, and starts to see who leads and who follows.
scene B: {N} means to show the whole family that seven children are nothing to {N}.
scene R: {N} has not had this much noise in the house in years and is enjoying every minute.
scene G: The house fills up the way it used to, coats on every hook and shoes on every stair.
- W | pin a rota of baths, jobs and bedtimes on the kitchen door | v: conformity, security | foot: lesson rotas save weekends | chance: 70
- U | find out what each child loves best and give each one a day of it | v: benevolence, self-direction | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 64
- B | put the eldest in charge, with a reward promised for keeping order | v: power, achievement | foot: door kept your word | chance: 66
- R | turn the front room into a fort of sheets and cushions | v: hedonism, stimulation | foot: means health-.03 | chance: 85
- G | cook one huge pot, sit them all at one table and let the noise come | v: tradition, benevolence | dream: test | foot: place gather.house | chance: 72
- W>G | keep the family's old bedtime story and song going for all seven | v: tradition, conformity | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 74
- U>W | work out a fair turn for the one bathroom and hold everyone to it | v: universalism, conformity | foot: lesson fair turns end the shouting | chance: 62
- B>U | strike a deal with the family next door to share the children between two houses | v: security, power | foot: person neighbour | chance: 60
- R>B | take all seven to the fair and win a prize for every one | v: stimulation, achievement | foot: means money-.05 | chance: 45
- G>R | take them all to the woods in the rain and let them run till dark | v: stimulation, universalism | dream: test | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 68
works: On the last night all seven fall asleep in a heap in the front room, and {N} sits up watching them.
works: When the parents come back, the children beg to stay another night.
fails: By the second day two of them are crying, one is sick, and {N} is counting the hours.
fails: A row between the two eldest spoils the weekend, and {sibling} hears about it from both.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to stay strong and well for life (G; cycle s2)

== the hill that wins every morning
tier: life event
aim: to stay strong and well for life
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-88
per_year: 0 .3 .4 .4 .4 .3
times: while the aim is set, a month of trying to beat one steep climb comes once or twice (estimate)
tone: mixed
life: health, nature
horizon: months
roles: friend, neighbour
earth: you have walked the steep hill behind the houses every morning for a month, and it still beats you
tribal: every dawn you climb the ridge above the camp with the water skins, and every dawn it still beats you
magic: every morning you climb the long stair of the old watchtower, and every morning it still beats you
scene: For a month {N} has walked up the hill behind the houses before the day begins, and every morning the hill wins: the last stretch, the pounding heart, the bench halfway that {N} swore never to sit on.
scene W: {N} has not missed a single morning yet, and is not going to start.
scene U: {N} has started to wonder what the body is actually doing on the climb, and why.
scene B: {N} has the time for every climb written down, and the times are not getting better fast enough.
scene R: {N} wants to tear up the hill just once, flat out, and see what happens.
scene G: At the top there is a view of the whole valley in the morning light, when {N} gets there.
- W | climb at the same hour every single morning, rain or shine | v: conformity, security | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 80
- U | read up on how bodies build strength, and make a plan of it | v: self-direction | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 74
- B | time every climb and beat the last one, every single day | v: achievement | foot: lesson numbers keep the climb honest | chance: 50
- R | run the whole hill flat out one morning, just to see | v: stimulation | body: light | foot: lesson rushing costs more than it gives | chance: 45
- G | walk slower, breathe with the steps and listen to the birds | v: universalism, security | dream: test | foot: means health+.05 | chance: 76
- W>B | join the early walking group and keep up with the fastest | v: achievement, conformity | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 58
- U>R | try a different sport each week until one sticks | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: place gather.games | chance: 62
- B>G | talk a friend into coming, so neither of them can skip a day | v: benevolence, achievement | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- R>W | dare the neighbour with the dog to a daily race to the top | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 66
- G>U | carry the walk on into the woods beyond and learn each tree on the way | v: universalism, self-direction | dream: test | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 72
works: One grey morning {N} reaches the top without stopping, and stands there laughing at nothing.
works: By the end of the season the bench halfway is just a bench, and {N} walks past it.
fails: A knee gives out on the steep part, and the doctor says to rest it for six weeks.
fails: The mornings get darker and colder, and one by one the climbs stop.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to care for those who cannot manage alone (G W; cycle s4)

== a week of looking in on someone
tier: life event
aim: to care for those who cannot manage alone
aim_role: spark
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-85
per_year: 0 .3 .4 .4 .4 .3
times: while the aim is set, a week of caring for a frail neighbour or relative comes once or twice (estimate)
tone: mixed
life: health, neighbours
horizon: week
roles: elder, a frail neighbour's family, a district nurse
earth: the old person two doors down can no longer manage alone, the family is far away, and you said you would look in
tribal: the old hunter by the far fire can no longer fetch his own water, and you said you would see to him
magic: the old scribe in the next room can no longer manage the stair, and you said you would bring what she needs
scene: {elder} from two doors down can no longer manage the stairs or the tablets, and the family is three hours away. For one week, {N} has said yes to looking in morning and night.
scene W: {N} promised the family on the phone, and a promise like that is kept.
scene U: {N} has no idea what the tablets are for, and that has to change by tonight.
scene B: {N} can see the family has no plan at all, and someone has to make one.
scene R: {N} finds {elder} sitting in the dark with the radio off, and cannot bear it.
scene G: {N} knows this street, and on this street nobody is left on their own.
- W | make a chart of the tablets and the meals, and tick off every visit | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 78
- U | ask the district nurse what to watch for, and write it all down | v: self-direction, benevolence | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 74
- B | ring the family and settle a fair price for the week's work | v: power, security | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 66
- R | bring the radio back on and dance a slow turn round the kitchen together | v: hedonism, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G | sit with them each evening, hold the cup, and let the hour be slow | v: benevolence | dream: test | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 76
- W>G | promise the family to keep coming after the week is out | v: benevolence, conformity | dream: test | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U>W | find out what help the council owes, and fill in the forms for them | v: universalism | foot: lesson help is there if asked | chance: 55
- B>U | get the agency to send a proper carer, and learn how it is done | v: security, achievement | foot: place care.houses | chance: 58
- R>B | ring the family and tell them straight that one week is not enough | v: benevolence, power | foot: lesson saying it plainly moves people | chance: 60
- G>R | wheel them out to the park they have not seen in years | v: benevolence, stimulation | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 64
works: By the end of the week {elder} is eating again, and asks if {N} will come on Sunday too.
works: The family rings to thank {N}, and the district nurse says {N} has a gift for this.
fails: {elder} has a fall on the fourth night while {N} is asleep at home, and it is a long week after that.
fails: {N} does what can be done, but it is too much for one pair of hands, and both of them know it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to feed the street from my garden (G W; cycle s1)

== more beans than one house can eat
tier: life event
aim: to feed the street from my garden
aim_role: spark
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 .4 .5 .4 .3
times: while the aim is set, a glut from the garden comes most summers (estimate)
tone: joy
life: home, neighbours, nature
horizon: week
roles: neighbour, friend, the café on the corner
earth: the beans and the marrows have all come at once, far more than one house can eat
tribal: the patch by the camp has given more roots and berries than one family can carry
magic: the walled bed has given three times what the kitchen can use, and it will not keep
scene: The beans and the marrows have come all at once, far more than one house could eat. The kitchen table is covered, the windowsill is covered, and there is more out there ripening by the hour.
scene W: {N} hates waste, and hates even more that the family on the corner is going short.
scene U: {N} wants to know why it all came at once, and how to spread next year's crop out.
scene B: {N} can see good money going soft on the windowsill.
scene R: {N} wants a feast, tonight, with everyone.
scene G: This is what a garden is for, {N} thinks: more than enough, to give away.
- W | set a box at the gate with a sign saying to take what is needed | v: universalism, benevolence | foot: lesson people take only what they need | chance: 82
- U | weigh the glut and plan next year's beds so nothing goes to waste | v: self-direction, security | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | sell the surplus from a table at the Saturday market | v: achievement | foot: place comm.market | chance: 64
- R | throw a supper out on the pavement with everything that is ripe | v: hedonism, benevolence | foot: means ties+.06 | chance: 66
- G | go door to door with a basket and leave something at every house | v: benevolence, tradition | dream: test | foot: person neighbour | chance: 78
- W>U | start a sign-up sheet so the street can share the work and the crop | v: universalism | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 56
- U>B | swap the surplus with the baker for bread right through the winter | v: security, achievement | foot: person keeper | chance: 60
- B>R | take a stall at the summer fair and make a show of the biggest marrow | v: hedonism, achievement | foot: place gather.great | chance: 58
- R>G | dig up the grass verge outside and plant it for anyone to pick | v: stimulation, universalism | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 50
- G>W | carry the best of it to the soup kitchen at the hall | v: benevolence | dream: test | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 76
works: By the weekend there is nothing left on the table, and three neighbours have asked for seeds.
works: The family on the corner sends back a jar of something wonderful made from the marrows.
fails: Half of it goes soft before anyone takes it, and {N} carries it to the compost heap.
fails: Someone complains about the mess at the gate, and the box has to come in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to belong to a congregation for life (G W; cycle s4)

== missed at worship for the first time
