magic: after two weeks away from the shrine, the fellowship at the gate asks where you have been
scene: {N} has been going to the same services for a season, sitting near the back. This week, after a fortnight away with a heavy cold, three people come over at the door to ask where {N} has been, and {elder} has kept {Ns} usual seat.
scene W: {N} feels the pull of the rota board by the door, the readings and the flowers and the soup.
scene U: {N} has been wondering for weeks what the oldest words of the service really mean.
scene B: {N} notices who runs things here, and how a newcomer might get a say.
scene R: {N} has been singing louder each week, and someone has noticed.
scene G: For the first time, the place feels like somewhere {N} belongs, not somewhere {N} visits.
