- U>W | read up on the old words of the services until they make sense | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: lesson the old words have reasons | chance: 66
- B>U | slip away before the greetings and keep a polite distance | v: security | dream: drop | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 85
- R>B | stand up at the members' meeting and push for a night for the young | v: stimulation, power | foot: person rival | chance: 52
- G>R | bring the whole family next week, children and all | v: tradition, stimulation | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 60
works: By the end of the month {N} is on first-name terms with half the congregation, and has a seat that is {Ns}.
works: {elder} says, at the door, that the place would not be the same without {N}, and means it.
fails: The warmth at the door fades by the next week, and {N} goes back to sitting at the back alone.
fails: An old quarrel between two families flares up over tea, and {N} is caught in the middle of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spark: to make a home everyone is welcome in (G W; cycle s1)

== dinner for nine and four chairs
