works: In the second spring the bed comes up thick and bright, and {N} stands at the window looking at it.
works: The neighbour leans over the fence and asks, a little put out, what {N} did to it.
fails: Whatever {N} tries, the bed stays bare, and by autumn it is put down to gravel.
fails: The new plants take for a month and then die back, all at once, in a hot week.

